title The set, not its size -- Tablecloth's nine refusals named and proven, and the meter that could not read its own museum
prompt The standing Silence seat: open on ListAgents and the cold roster, reds first, then the infrastructure half of Grain in Glow -- the vanes and services.
think Opened on ListAgents (one peer, grain-c0, interactive) and a clean tree. Reds first: construction/REDS.md carried one OPEN row, %354, whose Tablecloth half I repaired last lap and whose spool_cloth remainder is Pond's file, live with %341 -- another body's lane, so it surfaces like a gate rather than blocking my queue.
think Cold roster: 96 run, 94 green, 2 red, tree_at_open equal to tree_at_close. Both reds were already named on the card -- rule_twin is custody gate %7, pond_enclosure_door is Hush's. Last round's two nib guards had greened. No new red, so no standfast.
think Rota row 4 by N=3814 mod 5 -- Earth, Mercury, the concrete, the row whose sense is smell: the fact taken in whole at the door, before interpretation. Its fixed seat is Two Rooms, whose law is that only what a witness binds enters the checkable room as fact. Both governed the whole lap.
think The card's door for this lane was Tablecloth's nine ClothError paths on a count pedestal. Reading the two elder Tablecloth desks first, their guard's own header named the gap it was leaving: max_name and the nine ClothError paths wait for their own pedestals.
think Then the design question the Earth row asks. A count pedestal that displays 9 and is checked against a count of 9 agrees while the set underneath it has changed -- rename one path, or drop one and add another, and nine is still nine. That is %354's lesson one layer up: a bound on a value's LENGTH read as a bound on its ALPHABET, and here a set's SIZE read as the set.
think So the desk lists the nine names and the guard compares them as sorted sets. Two readings carry it, and I checked they can fire apart before writing both: the desk agrees with ITSELF (example equals how many names it lists) and the desk agrees with the RYE. Their conjunction gives count-agreement for free, so a third reading would have been a fourth copy of one fact -- the derived-spine rule's own warning about two readings that always fire together.
think Before building the pedestal I read what the module actually proves. The selftest exercised seven of the nine declared paths on metal; CatalogFull and Overflow were declared, returned in code at four sites, and never reached by any test. A pedestal claiming every refusal wears a name, standing over two names with no fact behind them, would be a monument built on a story.
think Measurement beats memory about my own first reading, twice this lap. I first suspected the exemplar brush-parse pedestal's guard never read its source at all; it does -- src_first_resident_witness.rish counts the ParseError block and asserts 13. What is true is narrower and still worth naming: it reads the count and three sampled names, so a rename among the other ten passes, and it writes the literal 13 inside the guard.
think Then grade-what-you-touch returned C+ 75 on the new pedestal, against a B door -- which under the QA rule pushes a molt frame. Before working that frame I graded the three elder desks. All four read exactly C+ 75. Four different documents do not grade identically, so the instrument was the suspect rather than the writing.
think Found it: tools/fixtures/q/qa_report_card.sh extracts a program's prose from lines opening // or #, the two marks REDS %276 named. Glow opens a comment with ::, and so do the .brush placards. The extractor emitted an empty file, measure() returned zeros, and the reach awk's zero-guard fired -- then that zero was SCORED. Register, one block earlier, correctly reports rather than scores below its floor; reach, which declares a hundred-word floor in the very next block, graded a reading of nothing.
obs Booked and closed as REDS %358, on the spine fetched from xy rather than read locally. Measured: 438 tracked .glow files and 8 .brush placards, all 34 residents of src/shape/ graded C+ 75 whatever they said. After teaching the extractor ::, the same four desks read A 92, B 83, C+ 75, A+ 98 -- the grades discriminate, which is the whole evidence that the reading is now a reading.
obs The C+ 75 that survives is now a REAL one: shape-brush-parse-error-count.glow at 66 words and reading grade 21 against a ceiling of 11. Sound's and Mind's desk, so it is named on the card rather than touched, together with its guard's literal example    13.
obs Both new readings proven from the refusing side, since a refusal proven only in the passing direction cannot be told from a bypass. The Tablecloth control grew from 19 cases to 28 -- 4 welcomes, 24 refusals, 0 wrong -- and case 21 is the one the set reading exists for: a path renamed in the Rye alone, count unchanged at nine on both sides, refused as error_names_disagree. Case 20 is its welcome: a tenth path added in all three rooms walks free, because the guard carries no roster of its own. The QA control gained five readings including the load-bearing one -- the same placard behind a mark the card does not know reads nothing.
obs The two unproven refusal paths are proven now, and both Overflow doors rather than one: render_manifest returns it at the header that will not fit and at the artifact line that will not fit after it, and a proof of one says nothing about the other. I checked the asserts are live rather than assuming it -- a deliberately false assert in a throwaway Rye file panics at exit 134 -- so each block proves the refusal AND its identity.
obs Hush's cross-bench falsifier is answered, and it splits cleanly. Their env normalization DID travel to this bench: env_disagreements=0. The door half did not: door_disagreements=1, one reading, user, derived=502 metal=unread, because the probe's uid $(id -u) returns empty through the reporter here while entry reads executable and /bin is reachable. Pond's file behind gate %5, so named rather than touched.
obs %354 stays OPEN rather than being re-read as BOOKED. Its remainder is genuinely a booked lap for another body, which fits the BOOKED definition, yet leaving it OPEN keeps it on the pin where Hush will meet it -- and re-classifying my own row one lap later is churn rather than tidiness.
obs The number collided on the send. I booked %357 from the fetched spine at 05:31 and Hush published their own %357 at 05:50, so the rebase met two rows wearing one number -- the exact class the derived-spine law was seated for. Theirs is on the anointed spine and frozen; mine was unshared, so mine renumbered to %358 and every citation moved with it. My stamp is the earlier of the two, and the number still went to the row that landed first, because the number is a view the remote allocates rather than a claim about when.
obs The card ran 589 bytes over its bound after the round's edits and came back under by dropping one landed line -- the Pond dialect bullet, whose %352 reads CLOSED and folded -- then condensing landed detail and tightening my own two blocks. No live fact of another body's was cut.
